#545 repair 3e -- PRE-TABLE CHECK, written BEFORE table 1 runs (this file's mtime is the order proof; run_r3e.sh logs
it first).  Scope: 3d's own pass (panel_20260923_202025: codex, grok, glm and kimi-k3:cloud DO NOT SHIP; agy, deepseek,
minimax SHIP; the kimi CLI weekly-walled, covered; the codex dedicated job, q2g/codex_ded, FAIL).  The Opus seat's
q2g pass is still running when this is written; its findings, if any, are adjudicated after this table.  The detector
is EXTENDED (no product change), so the block is owed.

THE CLASS-CLOSURE RULE APPLIES, and this repair is written to it: two consecutive passes each found a breach of the same
two classes --
  (A) a claimed-KEPT channel not read where the claim holds: 3c's pass, read nowhere (the Clear 0x20 row's status);
      3d's pass, read only at the END of a multi-access row (codex: `(d->irq_asserted ^= 1, !d->warned_irq_status_w)`
      toggles on every +0x180 decline, and the re-arm row's two batches cancel it);
  (B) the handler's use of the caller's buffer beyond `len`: 3c's pass, the fetch (deepseek, FW1 -> E5); 3d's pass, the
      read write-back (kimi-k3:cloud) -- and a real ARM narrow load passes data[1]/data[2]/data[4]
      (cpu_arm_instr_loadstore.c:104-126), so a wider write-back overflows the caller's buffer.
Each is closed as a CLASS in this one diff:
  (A) X14's multi-access rows (the DEVINIT declines rows and the re-arm row -- every other X14 row makes one access, so
      its end IS the access) check all five fields (irq_status, irq_enable, fiq_status, fiq_enable, irq_asserted) after
      EACH decline (ZDECLINE: a snapshot at entry, ZKEPT after each call), after each legal read and after the Clear.
  (B) X6 (every declined access, every width, both directions), X9 and X10 (every legal read, every width) check the
      bytes above the width are still the 0xa5 fill (pad_kept).  X11/X12/X13's reads are len-4 declines with the class
      carried at every width by X6/X9/X10 -- recorded here, not an omission.
and the two disclosures 3d's pass found one axis short are widened to their classes, in the contract's NOT COVERED:
  the CALLER context (grok: the calloc'd cpu's byte order, pc 0 -- beyond `mem` and the machine type): "a condition on
    ANY caller state"; the Clear's DESTINATION (codex dedicated: keyed on `fiq_enable & 1`, at len 4): "keyed on the
    width or on a field X14's instances do not vary".
Records: E3's reason (1 after the DEASSERTING Clear pins the defect; after the asserting Clear 0x400 it is right, and
the re-arm row pins that -- codex, codex dedicated); the 0xa5 fill's reason (poison, not "a real store's bytes"; codex,
codex dedicated); FS02's condition (grok, codex); "five checks" -> six named rows at four check sites (codex).

1. SIBLING PARITY -- the DEVINIT declines rows and the re-arm row share ZDECLINE: both get the per-decline check.  The
   re-arm row's reads and Clear get it too; the DEVINIT reads and Set/Clear rows claim values and the drive, not kept
   fields -- unchanged.  X6/X9/X10 get pad_kept together; X12/X13 already fill (E5).
2. CLAIM -> ROW -- COVERED "every field and irq_asserted checked after EACH decline" -> the DEVINIT declines rows
   (R3E_CXT1); "checked after EACH of its access" -> the re-arm row (R3E_CXT1); "the bytes above the width untouched
   (X6, X9, X10)" -> R3E_WB4.  NOT COVERED widenings -> no row, measured as controls: R3E_BO1, R3E_PC1 (caller),
   R3E_CXD1 (destination).  glm's two premise shapes (does X12/X13 read the FIQ fields; does X6 read the four) ->
   R3E_GLM1, R3E_GLM2, expected red on BOTH instruments.
3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD -- N/A: no product line or guard changes.  The new conjuncts read the five fields, whose
   writers are known (irq_status/irq_asserted: the producer pair only; fiq_status: none; the enables: their arms):
   none changes during a decline or a legal read in the fix, and the re-arm's Clear 0x400 leaves 0x10 & ~0x400 = 0x10.
4. CHANNEL -- per new check, the mutant it kills and the observable that differs:
   ZKEPT after each decline, DEVINIT rows   R3E_CXT1  irq_asserted 0 -> 1 after the +0x180 decline      (r3d green)
   ZKEPT after each decline, re-arm row     R3E_CXT1  irq_asserted 1 -> 0 after the first batch's +0x180 (r3d green)
   ZKEPT after each read / the Clear        a read that sets a field the Clear then restores -- the channel can
                                            vary; no dedicated shape is built (the per-decline form is the measured one)
   pad_kept, X6/X9/X10                      R3E_WB4   b[w..3] after a len-1/2 read: 0xa5 -> odata's bytes (r3d green)
   None is vacuous by construction.
5. ROWS PRESCRIBED BY THE PRIOR BLOCK (PRETABLE_Q2e.out) -- diffed: E1-E5 all present, no row removed or renamed.
PRETABLE_Q2F_DONE
